{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in compact deterministic specifications. The policy gives strong forward bias in clear space, uses one-shot recovery states after obstacle events, keeps uncontrollable events total in every spec state, treats obstacle events as safety-critical preemptions in action states, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort stuck state only.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensor outcomes and motion capabilities into plant automata, then bind perception states to exactly one intended controllable action via specifications.",
    "Use one-shot commit/recovery states so open-loop pulses remain safe: path_clear usually self-loops in action states, while obstacle events preempt to obstacle-recovery states; after recovery, return quickly to forward exploration."
  ],
